cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAG chunking strategies, with confidence intervals"
message: "If you use this benchmark or its question set, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vaishnavi
    family-names: Sonawane
repository-code: "https://github.com/vaishnavi-sonawane27/RAG-Chunking-Strategies"
abstract: >-
  A small, fully reproducible comparison of five document chunking strategies
  (fixed-size, fixed-size with overlap, sentence-based, recursive and semantic)
  for retrieval in RAG pipelines. Uses a 215-question evaluation set covering all
  64 sections of the openly licensed Pro Git book (~107k words), a held-out
  dev/test split so chunk
  sizes are not tuned on the reported data, and paired bootstrap confidence
  intervals so that differences between strategies can be assessed for
  significance rather than ranked on point estimates alone.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - chunking
  - information retrieval
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
